---
---

<header class="hero">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Raw NASA light curves, not the Kaggle set</p>
    <h1>Finding real planets in raw telescope data</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A from-scratch transit-detection pipeline: pull raw photometry from NASA's public archive, detrend it,
      run the same classical search astronomers use, and check the answers against known planets before pointing
      it at real, unconfirmed candidates.
    </p>
    <div class="animation-frame">
      <img
        src="/images/trappist1b_sync_animation.gif"
        alt="A simulated planet crossing a simulated star, synced to the real dip in TRAPPIST-1's light curve"
        width="1160"
        height="480"
      />
    </div>
    <p class="caption">
      TRAPPIST-1 b: a simulated transit (physically sized to the real ~0.7% depth) synced to the actual,
      detrended K2 light curve, phase-folded at the period this pipeline recovered on its own.
    </p>
  </div>
</header>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 88px 0 56px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.2vw, 3rem);
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto 0.4em;
  }
  .lede {
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: 0 auto 40px;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
  }
  .animation-frame {
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg-panel);
  }
  .animation-frame img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }
  .caption {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 16px auto 0;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
</style>
